# Bibliography - DATS 6401 Project 1

## APA Citation Format Guide

Below are templates for citing different types of sources in APA format.

---

## Data Sources (Required)

### Dataset A
[Author/Organization]. (Year). *Dataset name* [Data set]. Source Name. URL

**Example:**
U.S. Census Bureau. (2023). *American Community Survey 5-year estimates* [Data set]. United States Census Bureau. https://data.census.gov/

### Dataset B
[Author/Organization]. (Year). *Dataset name* [Data set]. Source Name. URL

---

## Journal Articles

### Template
Author, A. A., Author, B. B., & Author, C. C. (Year). Title of article. *Title of Periodical, volume*(issue), page range. https://doi.org/xxxxx

### Example
Smith, J. D., & Johnson, K. L. (2023). The impact of climate change on agricultural productivity. *Journal of Environmental Economics, 45*(3), 234-256. https://doi.org/10.1234/jee.2023.45.3.234

---

## Books

### Template
Author, A. A. (Year). *Title of work: Capital letter also for subtitle*. Publisher Name. https://doi.org/xxxxx

### Example
Tufte, E. R. (2001). *The visual display of quantitative information* (2nd ed.). Graphics Press.

---

## Book Chapters

### Template
Author, A. A., & Author, B. B. (Year). Title of chapter. In E. E. Editor (Ed.), *Title of book* (pp. xxx-xxx). Publisher.

---

## Government/Agency Reports

### Template
Agency Name. (Year). *Title of report* (Report No. xxx). Publisher. URL

### Example
U.S. Department of Agriculture. (2024). *Agricultural statistics 2024* (Report No. USDA-2024-01). U.S. Government Publishing Office. https://www.usda.gov/reports/agricultural-statistics

---

## Online Articles/News

### Template
Author, A. A. (Year, Month Day). Title of article. *Publication Name*. URL

### Example
Jones, M. (2024, January 15). Rising trends in renewable energy adoption. *The New York Times*. https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/15/science/renewable-energy.html

---

## Websites

### Template
Author/Organization. (Year, Month Day). *Title of webpage*. Site Name. URL

### Example
National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration. (2024, March 10). *Climate change indicators*. NOAA Climate.gov. https://www.climate.gov/maps-data/climate-data-primer/climate-change-indicators

---

## Working Papers/Preprints

### Template
Author, A. A. (Year). *Title of working paper* (Working Paper No. xxx). Institution. URL

---

## Your References (Minimum 6 Required)

1. [Dataset A Citation]

2. [Dataset B Citation]

3. [Source that inspired your topic]

4. [Credible source supporting your analysis]

5. [Credible source providing context]

6. [Additional credible source]

7. [Additional source if needed]

8. [Additional source if needed]

---

## BibTeX Format (Optional - for LaTeX users)

```bibtex
@dataset{census2023acs,
  author = {{U.S. Census Bureau}},
  title = {American Community Survey 5-year Estimates},
  year = {2023},
  publisher = {United States Census Bureau},
  url = {https://data.census.gov/}
}

@article{smith2023climate,
  author = {Smith, John D. and Johnson, Karen L.},
  title = {The Impact of Climate Change on Agricultural Productivity},
  journal = {Journal of Environmental Economics},
  volume = {45},
  number = {3},
  pages = {234--256},
  year = {2023},
  doi = {10.1234/jee.2023.45.3.234}
}

@book{tufte2001visual,
  author = {Tufte, Edward R.},
  title = {The Visual Display of Quantitative Information},
  edition = {2nd},
  publisher = {Graphics Press},
  year = {2001}
}
```

---

## In-Text Citation Examples

### Single Author
(Smith, 2023)
Smith (2023) found that...

### Two Authors
(Smith & Johnson, 2023)
Smith and Johnson (2023) demonstrated...

### Three or More Authors
(Smith et al., 2023)
Smith et al. (2023) showed...

### Organization as Author
(U.S. Census Bureau, 2023)
According to the U.S. Census Bureau (2023)...

### No Author
(*Title of Work*, 2023)

### Direct Quote
(Smith, 2023, p. 45)
Smith (2023) stated that "direct quote here" (p. 45).

---

## Credible Sources Checklist

✓ Peer-reviewed academic journals
✓ Government agencies and official statistics
✓ Reputable research institutions
✓ Established news organizations
✓ Professional associations
✓ University publications
✓ Think tanks and research centers

✗ Wikipedia (can use for background, but cite original sources)
✗ Personal blogs
✗ Social media posts
✗ Non-peer-reviewed sources without verification

